<article class="env-notation" id="84D07D">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/84D07D">Notation <span data-tag="84D07D">4.2.3.1</span>.</a>KF@$K_{F}$ We define a simplicial set $K_{F}$ as follows. A map $\Delta ^ n \rightarrow K_{F}$ is determined by the following data: </p>
  <p><ul>
  <li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(i)$"><p>
A map $\Delta ^{n} \rightarrow \Delta ^{1}$, corresponding to a decomposition $[n] = \{  0, \ldots , i \}  \cup \{  i+1, \ldots , n\} $. 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(ii)$"><p>
A map $e_{-}: \Delta ^{ \{  0, \ldots , i\}  } \rightarrow K$. 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(iii)$"><p>
A map $e_{+}: \Delta ^{\{  i+1, \ldots , n\}  } \rightarrow \Nerve (\calI )$, which we may view as a chain of composable morphisms 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  I(i+1) \rightarrow \ldots \rightarrow I(n) \]
</div>
<p>
 in the category $\calI $. 
</p>
</li><li class="custom-item" data-marker="$(iv)$"><p>
For each $j \in \{ i+1, \ldots , n\} $, a map $e_{j}$ which fits into a commutative diagram 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \xymatrix { &amp;  K_{I(j)} \ar [d]^{\pi _{I(j)}} \\ \Delta ^{ \{ 0, \ldots , i\}  } \ar [r]^{e_{-}} \ar [ur]^{e_ j} &amp;  K} \]
</div>
<p>
 Moreover, for $j \leq k$ we require that $e_ k$ is given by the composition 
</p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \Delta ^{ \{ 0, \ldots , i\}  } \stackrel{ e_ j }{\rightarrow } K_{I(j)} \rightarrow K_{I(k)}. \]
</div>
</li>
</ul></p>
</article>